#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:1
msgid "Data Files You Need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:4
msgid "PySME uses local cache data under `~/.sme/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:6
msgid ""
"The supported way to change data/cache locations is to edit "
"`~/.sme/config.json`. PySME reads directory settings from that file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:9
msgid "Typical files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:11
msgid "Atmosphere grids"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:12
msgid "NLTE grids"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:13
msgid "Optional custom resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:15
msgid "Configure data locations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:17
msgid "Edit `~/.sme/config.json` and set the data paths you want:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:35
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:37
msgid ""
"`data.file_servers` is optional and defines an ordered list of path-"
"compatible mirrors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:38
msgid ""
"If `data.file_servers` is present, PySME expands relative pointer paths "
"against those servers and falls back automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:39
msgid ""
"If `data.file_servers` is absent, PySME uses legacy `data.file_server` "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:40
msgid "Pointer values in `datafiles_*.json` can be:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:41
msgid ""
"a single relative path (expanded against each path-compatible mirror "
"server)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:42
msgid "a list of paths/URLs (tried in order)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:43
msgid "a full URL (`https://...` or `file://...`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:44
msgid ""
"Absolute URLs are tried as written and are not joined with "
"`data.file_servers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:45
msgid ""
"This allows mixed-source fallbacks such as `NADC -> Uppsala -> Zenodo` in"
" a single pointer list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:46
msgid ""
"In the current PySME defaults, Uppsala is configured as the path-"
"compatible mirror in `data.file_servers`, while NADC and Zenodo are "
"usually referenced as explicit URLs in the pointer files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:47
msgid ""
"The NADC packaged data mirror page is <https://nadc.china-"
"vo.org/res/r101793/>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:48
msgid ""
"`~` is supported in path values and will be expanded to your home "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:49
msgid ""
"Changing these paths does not migrate old files automatically; move "
"existing files manually if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:51
msgid "Accessing data files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:52
msgid ""
"The atmosphere and nlte data files should be downloaded from the server "
"automatically when used, so network connection is required when using "
"PySME (not only during installation). These files can also be downloaded "
"manually by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:54
msgid ""
"Download data files as part of IDL SME from "
"[here](http://www.stsci.edu/~valenti/sme.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:55
msgid ""
"copy them into their respective storage locations in ~/.sme/atmospheres "
"and ~/.sme/nlte_grids"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:56
msgid "atmospheres: everything from SME/atmospheres"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:57
msgid ""
"Download the nlte_grids in "
"[zenodo](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3888393)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/data_files.md:58
msgid ""
"The files (mainly atmosphere models and NLTE departure coefficient grids)"
" required by PySME will be saved inside `~/.sme/`. These files can be "
"large thus if your home directory is small, we recommend to create a "
"softlink for `~/.sme`."
msgstr ""

